owever anytime we mention gyro i do  need to do the standard explanation  which is that in the anime an  extraordinarily important part was cut  out of the chimera ant arc and that was  when  gyro was shown alive after having been  converted into chimera ant and  sinisterly strolling through the very  same city that both gon and kilwa were  present in and currently it's believed  that gyro is in meteor city however the  reason why he is on this list is because  he presents  quite possibly the greatest potential  threat that this series has ever known  and this is because during his flashback  we saw that gyro was an individual who  had cast aside his humanity  long before becoming a chimera ant and  his sole goal in life is now simply to  disseminate evil throughout the world  and his tenacity for this evil is so  strong that it allowed him to easily  break free of the ant queen's control  and retain his human memories  so now with his new body and the  potential of nenus which as we know  responds directly to desire  gyro is very much the ultimate  antagonist just waiting to rock this  world and the only reason why he's this  far down on the list is because we've  only seen the briefest of glimpses of  that however that one glimpse is more  than enough to land him at number eight  more manga specific stuff now as we head  into number seven with beyond netara a  man who inherited almost 100  of his aesthetics from his father isaac  nataro along with what is hinted to be  an astonishing level of power and a  startling amount of charisma however  beyond puts these traits to use in a  much more outwardly antagonistic way  than his father ever did and at this  very moment beyond is almost  single-handedly spearheading the plot to  travel to the dark continent  a location that he has already been to  on one occasion mind you which speaks  pretty tremendously to his capabilities  something that is quite underrated  regarding beyond though is his mental  prowess he is a man who has managed to  outwit  each and every one of the zodiacs within  the hunter association as well as entire  structures of power such as the kakin  empire or the v5 nations  and essentially resulting in beyond  having managed to manipulate every  primary source of political power in the  human realm simply to achieve his own  highly mysterious dark continent-related  goals  which whatever they are they are not  good this man is the embodiment of  sinister and right now it's really  difficult to think of anyone who would  be able to stop him so to turn away from  that impending disaster let's all focus  on number six being hisoka and honestly  compared to every other antagonist we've  explored thus far and will continue to  explore hisoka really doesn't compare in  terms of motivation he's just a morally  ambiguous clown magician out there to do  nothing but satisfy his own lust for  combat  and that makes him so consistently  inconsistent hisoka is an antagonist who  is capable of assuming any role in story  he can serve as the main antagonist as  he effectively did during the hunter  exam in heaven's arena but he can also  be a supporting character like york new  city or even a protagonist himself like  on greed island but the important thing  here is that we  as an audience never quite know how this  is going to pan out it's very hard to  predict which hisokui will be served and  as such despite the fact that his  actions are you know  less world shaking than others his  strong history within the series and  continued menace absolutely makes him  one of the most fearsome antagonists  that hunter hunter has to offer but  speaking of fearsome i think that one  antagonist that really embodies that  word would be our number five  nephipito from the moment that pito  first stepped into the series hunter  hunter was hit with a wave of  unstoppable primal force  in fact i would actually describe pito  as a hisoka just with a goal that is not  entirely selfish  which in my eyes makes pito far far more  dangerous  when it comes down to it peter will do  anything and everything for the sake of  the ant king and they'll have a hell of  a lot of fun doing it as well which of  course  includes wild amounts of sadistic  torture hurrah pepito also comes  equipped with other troubling qualities  such as an effectively unlimited  quantity of aura and an affinity of  specialization which putting the two  together means that pito is capable of  accomplishing anything and  everything that they please very much  disturbing the balance of the nen power  system by putting the unlimited aura  cheat on but of course beta also comes  with a deep emotional connection as an  antagonist due to the whole kite killing  fiasco an action that would eventually  result in our main protagonist gone  being removed from the focus of the  series altogether so really when you  think about it that's a pretty stunning  endorsement of peter an antagonist that  really did put an end to our main  character with that said hunter hunter  has a fair bit more to offer including  our number four crolo lucifer so  initially he has the whole stoic silent  illumi vibe about him except that crollo  is demonstrably more driven  as the leader of the phantom troop  crawler has command over one of the  single most powerful group of  individuals on the planet and he puts  them to pretty phenomenal use because  crawler is what i would describe  as utility combatant on his own he does  not present power in a classical sense  and his danger mainly comes from his  ability to analyze and strategize which  is of course very well reflected in his  non-ability skill hunter allowing him to  steal the abilities of others but only  after fulfilling a truly ridiculous  amount of conditions that only someone  of crolo level genius would be able to  pull off and as such with the right  amount of planning i firmly believe that  crolo could defeat anyone  something that was demonstrated in the  manga in his very one-sided fight  against hisoka in heaven's arena however  this also highlights a great weakness  because crollo is far less adept at  improvised combat without a  well-formulated strategy he is quite  vulnerable but then again  only to really top tnn users with plenty  of time for strategy though crollo  may as well be invincible maybe  invincible depends who is going up  against that is because there are other  incredibly sharp minds in the series and  one of the most finely tuned would be  our number three pariston hill and i  have never been more terrified by a  character that we know next to nothing  about  than i have with paristan every time he  appears on screen or on page he makes me  very very nervous and for good reason as  well because you can never quite dissect  paristan's goals or feelings even when  he has inner monologues because they  generally leave me with more  questions and answers and just an  overwhelming takeaway of no one  no one ever should be around this man he  is an unequivocal danger to everyone and  everything and this happy facade will  always instill more fear into me than  even the creepiest expressions of  someone like pito hisoko or illumi  none of them have anything on this  terrifyingly happy man  with that said if i had to choose i  would much rather be around paristan  than our number two contender  fourth prince charadnick because of all  of the monsters that togashi has  conjured sradnik would be the most  concerning as he really does push the  desires of humanity far beyond any  reasonable limits and really kind of  crosses over into the territory of being  demonic i mean his hobbies are the kind  of things that we would see happening in  like a 15th century painting of hell and  that's because saradnik has by far the  scariest hobby of all  which is art and humans are merely  supplies for said art and perhaps that  wouldn't be so bad on its own however in  addition to this radnic just so happens  to be quite possibly the greatest  natural net genius that we've ever  casually stumbled across  easily eclipsing the talon to both gon  and kilauea who were both said to have a  one in ten million talent and if that is  indeed the metric we're going by then  saradnick would easily be one in a  billion aura control just comes so  naturally to him that before even having  mastered the basics of nen he had  already unconsciously summoned his onan  beast as well as developed a separate  hatsu that allows him to see briefly  into the future oh and he is of course a  specialist which always makes things  much  much worse if left unchecked for a few  more days let alone weak support the  blackwell one  i have no doubt that sradnik will become  one of the greatest nin users in the  world which will signal the beginning of  a very dark age for those within his  wide reaching radius but still it is  very difficult to crown him as the  ultimate antagonist given that we do  have  number one the ant king meruem the  literal antagonist if you will  although to be fair i also could have  made that joke with both pito and gyro  but i  saved it for the king because i really  cannot do this character any degree of  justice in a short explanation like this  but for a creature who began life as an  overpowered cell rip-off he developed  into one of the most compelling  presences in this  and indeed any other series meroem is an  antagonist so well written  that it generally makes me question  whether we were on the right side during  the chimera antarctic and whether or not  the world would actually be a better  place perhaps even as close as we could  come to a utopia with him in charge  he was simultaneously fear-inducing and  yet incredibly empathetic  to the point where it was tragic to see  him depart existence because he had  learnt so much more and come so much  further in 40 days than the entire human  race had in their long long history and  so to me  marowan will always be the greatest  antagonist and quite possibly arguably  even the greatest protagonist of hunter  hunter but what do you guys think please  do leave your thoughts in the comments  below or even join my discord server and  if you're keen for some more hand toned  content then please do go and check out  some of my other videos or even  subscribe to the channel for regular  hunt hunter glory delivered straight  into your youtube feed but for now this  has been the new world review  and i'll see you next time

